-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",167,{
[5313]="700280A4\n1\tDefeat Knotfist, the leader of the Abominations\tBlaire wants you to defeat Knotfist and end the Abominations once and for all.\n2\tTalk to Blaire\tHaving defeated the Abomination leader, Knotfist, speak with Blaire outside Lhan Colvarn once you have left the instance.\n",
[5314]="70037E27\n1\tCollect slabs of boar-meat (total: 4)\tGather the meat from four boars. Boars wander the hills east of the Folde Farm.\n2\tTalk to Athelbald\tAthelbald is at the Folde Farm. You should bring the boar-meat that you collected to Athelbald.\n",
[5315]="700169B7\n1\tThere are many dwarves at the Orc-watch. Róarr was surprised at Nykr's passing. While he did not know why his friend valued this little hand-made locket so highly, he suggested you question the other dwarves at the Orc-Watch.\t\n2\tTalk to Róarr at the Orc-watch\tRóarr is in the Orc-Watch. Róarr will want to hear of the locket's significance, so that he can relay the information back to Gufi.\n",
[5316]="70032C2B\n1\tThere are many dwarves at the Orc-watch. Róarr was surprised at Nykr's passing. While he did not know why his friend valued this little hand-made locket so highly, he suggested you question the other dwarves at The Orc-Watch.\t\n2\tTalk to Róarr at the Orc-watch\tRóarr is in the Orc-Watch. Róarr will want to hear of the locket's significance, so that he can relay the information back to Gufi.\n",
[5317]="7002C60B\n1\tRescue Finnvarth\tYou should find Finnvarth the dwarf and help him get back to the mill. Armund suggested that he should have been exploring somewhere not far to the east of the old sawmill in the Limlight Gorge.\n2\tTalk to Finnvarth\tYou should speak with Finnvarth at the Limlight Gorge sawmill.\n",
[5318]="70046BB7\n1\tMeet with Mithrandir\tYou should talk to Mithrandir at the road that leads to the Morgul Vale, near to the after-battle Cross-roads.\n2\tTalk to Mithrandir\tYou should talk to Mithrandir at the road that leads to the Morgul Vale, near to the after-battle Cross-roads.\n3\tTalk to Angbor\tYou should talk to Angbor, who can be found at the Cross-roads.\n",
[5319]="70068365\n1\tCollect worm fire-glands ([see journal]/6)\tYou were instructed to head north and west of the expedition encampment to find the intact fire-glands in the throats of the worms there. When gathered, you should return the glands to Abido at the expedition camp.\n2\tTalk to Abido\030Collect Worm Gland (total: 6)\tYou recovered the intact fire-glands from the worms in the eastern area of the Cape of Umbar. Return your collection to Abido at the hunter's expedition in the south-east of the Cape of Umbar.\n",
[5320]="7002659E\n1\tBurn the boats (total: 4)\tOrchalwë wants you to burn the boats at the dock.\n2\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë will want to know the boats have been burned.\n",
[5321]="7003FFF4\n1\tSet fuses (total: 3)\tSinking a corsair ship will cripple their occupation.\n",
[5322]="70066276\n1\tDiscover the camp of Dâr Matum\tThere are many spider eggs waiting to hatch in Dâr Matum.\n2\tBurn spider eggs (total: 6)\tThere are many spider eggs waiting to hatch in Dâr Matum. Set fire to spider eggs.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have burned many spider eggs.\n",
[5323]="7002658E\n1\tBurn the supply tents (total: 2)\tThe two large tents supply the eastern gate forces with supplies.\n2\tTalk to Orchalwë\tOrchalwë will be pleased to hear that the tents are ablaze.\n",
[5324]="700300D7\n1\tCollect glands from salamanders (total: 8)\tSalamanders are found just north of Harwick in the swamps along the road outside of the city. You should collect glands from salamanders to help the refugees keep their fires lit for protection against the dark and cold.\n2\tBring Cadda the salamander glands (but do keep it a secret)\tCadda is at the refugee camp outside of Harwick, waiting to grow tall so that he may be a great warrior of Rohan. You should bring the salamander glands to Cadda, but naturally keeping it a great secret, for the child wishes to take all the credit. How can you refuse?\n",
[5325]="7005479D\n1\tStart fires throughout Emyn Duir to distract the Enemy (total: 10)\030Defeat foes in Emyn Duir (total: 12)\tFlammable debris can be found throughout Emyn Duir. You should start fires and defeat enemies throughout Emyn Duir.\n2\tTalk to Nithi\tNithi can be found at Barthost. You should return to Nithi with news of your successes in Emyn Duir.\n",
[5326]="700442B5\n1\tPick up a water bucket in the besieged city\tA burning stone landed in the Sixth Circle. Rathon wanted you to pick up a water bucket and use that to extinguish the stone. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n2\tPick up a water bucket in the besieged city\tA burning stone landed in the Fifth Circle. Rathon wanted you to find a water bucket and use that to extinguish the stone. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n3\tPick up a water bucket in the besieged city\tA burning stone landed in the Fourth Circle. Rathon wanted you to find a water bucket and use that to extinguish the stone. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n4\tTalk to Forlong in the Fourth Circle of the besieged city\030Talk to Golasgil in the Fourth Circle of the besieged city\tForlong and Golasgil are in the Fourth Circle of the besieged city, and have sought to get your attention. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n5\tPick up a water bucket in the besieged city\tA burning stone landed in the Third Circle. Rathon wanted you to find a water bucket and use that to extinguish the stone. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n6\tPick up a water bucket in the besieged city\tA burning stone landed in the Second Circle. Rathon wanted you to find a water bucket and use that to extinguish the stone. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n7\tTalk to Duinhir in the Second Circle of the besieged city\tDuinhir and his sons are in the Second Circle of the besieged city, and have sought to get your attention. Minas Tirith is besieged! You may examine the model of the city in the Dome of the Sun to travel between states of the city.\n",
[5327]="700372CD\n1\tYou should defeat as many of the Warg-rider defilers as possible.\tWarg-riders from Isengard ride to and fro throughout the Broadacres, burning the fields as they go. You should defeat as many of the Warg-rider defilers as possible.\n2\tDefeat Warg-rider defilers (total: 6)\tWarg-riders from Isengard ride to and fro throughout the western fields of the Broadacres, burning the fields as they go. You should defeat as many of the Warg-rider defilers as possible.\n",
[5328]="7004962A\n1\tDefeat fire grims, Ghâsh-hai, and flame-spirits in Nargroth\tNargroth is located in Talath Úrui. You should defeat fire grims, Ghâsh-hai, and flame-spirits in Nargroth.\n2\tDefeat Fire Grims in Nargroth (total: 4)\030Defeat Ghâsh-hai in Nargroth (total: 10)\030Defeat Flame-spirits in Nargroth (total: 4)\tNargroth is located in Talath Úrui. You should defeat fire grims, Ghâsh-hai, and flame-spirits in Nargroth.\n3\tCompleted\tDefeated many fire grims, Ghâsh-hai, and flame-spirits in Nargroth.\n",
[5329]="700494D0\n1\tDefeat Fumaroles (total: 6)\030Defeat Fire Grims (total: 8)\tFumaroles and Fire Grims can be found in Talath Úrui, mainly near the Ghâshghurm. You should defeat any Fumaroles and Fire Grims that you encounter.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many Fumaroles and Fire Grims in Talath Úrui.\n",
[5330]="70008141\n1\tCollect driftwood (total: 6)\030Collect firewood (total: 6)\tFirewood and driftwood can be found near Ost Lagoros. You should collect firewood and driftwood to help Orthonn keep his fire burning hot.\n2\tReturn to Orthonn\tOrthonn is at his camp-site on the south-eastern edge of Annúndir. You should bring the firewood to Orthonn.\n",
[5331]="7002BBB6\n1\tLaunch blue fireworks at the firework show in Bree\030Launch red fireworks at Frérin's Court in Ered Luin\030Launch green fireworks at the entrance to the Last Homely House\030Launch orange fireworks at the peak of Weathertop in the Lonelands\030Launch yellow fireworks at the Party Tree in the Shire\030Launch purple fireworks at Tom Bombadil's house in the Old Forest\tGandalf has asked you to travel to each of these locations and launch the appropriate fireworks: Launch blue fireworks at the firework show in Bree, near the North-gate. Launch red fireworks at Frérin's Court outside of Thorin's Hall. Launch green fireworks at the Last Homely House in Rivendell. Launch yellow fireworks at the Party Tree of Hobbiton in the Shire. Launch orange fireworks at the summit of Weathertop in the Lone-lands. Launch purple fireworks outside Tom Bombadil's home in the Old Forest.\n2\tReturn to Gandalf at the Methel-stage fireworks show\tGandalf may be found at the Methel-stage north of Bywater in the Shire during the firework shows. You should return to Gandalf and share with him your experiences with fireworks.\n",
[5332]="70009C22\n1\tTalk to Robert Greenverge\030Collect dwarf-fireworks (quantity: see journal)\030Collect Elf-fireworks (quantity: see journal)\030Collect hobbit-fireworks (quantity: see journal)\030Collect Man-fireworks (quantity: see journal)\tThe fireworks vendors can be found in Duillond, Thorin's Halls, the Party Tree, and the Bree Festival Grounds. Robert Greenverge awaits you at the Bree Festival Grounds. Robert Greenverge has asked you to gather the four special fireworks from the fireworks vendors of Summerdays. Time is of the essence.\n",
[5333]="7002AF4A\n1\tLaunch the correct firework (total: 10)\tThe fireworks area is found near the North-gate of Bree. You should launch the correct fireworks as the conductor calls out the colour.\n2\tTalk to Winston Peartree\tWinston Peartree is at the fireworks area near the North-gate of Bree. You should talk to Winston Peartree about your performance in the fireworks show.\n",
[5334]="7002B308\n1\tWait for the announcer to declare the start of the show\tFirework launchers have been placed on the Methel-stage, north of Bywater in the Shire. You should wait for the announcer to declare the start of the event, then launch as many fireworks as you can. NOTE: You will need more than one or two participants in order to launch enough fireworks to amuse the crowd.\n2\tLaunch fireworks to impress the crowd\tThe fireworks launchers are on the Methel-stage, north of Bywater, in the Shire. You should use the fireworks-launcher to put on a wonderful show for the crowd. The best way to entertain the crowd is to work with others and set off as many fireworks as you can. NOTE: You will need more than one or two participants in order to launch enough fireworks to amuse the crowd. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Milo Brockhouse at the Methel-stage\tMilo Brockhouse is at the Methel-stage, north of Bywater, in the Shire. You should speak with Milo Brockhouse about your efforts in the Shire fireworks show.\n",
[5335]="7000AB88\n1\tBring the First Age Relic to Ásgeir\030Collect First Age relic\tSarnúr lies south of Thorin's Hall and west of Noglond in the ruins of Orodost. Ásgeir has asked you to enter the Dourhand stronghold of Sarnúr and defeat the creatures who dwell there, claiming First Age relics for the dwarves of Thorin's Hall.\n",
[5336]="7000874C\n1\tReturn to Chieftain Durulkum at Dâr-gazag\030Collect a First Marshals' mark\tFirst Marshals can only be found in towers and keeps claimed by the enemy. Chieftain Durulkum at Dâr-gazag informed you that the marks borne by the First Marshals of the enemy army gain great favour with Mordirith in Angmar.\n",
[5337]="70068BFD\n1\tCollect casks of mead from the gut (total: 6)\tIbzan has asked you to take back casks of mead stolen from Corsairs in the Gut.\n2\tTalk to Ibzan at the Black Anchor\tYou have taken back as many casks as you can from the Corsairs of the Gut.\n",
[5338]="70041185\n1\tAid Harnion in weakening the forces in Tarlang's Crown\tYou should continue to weaken the forces of Tarlang's Crown. Harnion has asked you to weaken the forces of Tarlang's Crown before confronting Azruthor. Completing the deed Quests of Tarlang's Crown will advance this quest.\n2\tTalk to Harnion\tHarnion can be found along the road into Tarlang's Crown from Belfalas. Harnion has asked you to weaken the forces of Tarlang's Crown before confronting Azruthor. You should now speak to Harnion.\n3\tTalk to Elaglar in Dol Amroth\tElaglar can be found in the Court of the Fount in Dol Amroth. You should speak to Elaglar about your first victory against the Heirs of Castamir.\n",
[5339]="70043B47\n1\tCollect marshy taters in the middle of the Drownholt (total: 6)\030Collect bushels of sage at the Wild Ruin, south of Ost Galadh (total: 4)\030Collect meat from crows throughout Mirkwood, especially in Emyn Lûm (total: 5)\030Collect sprigs of mint from around the tower of Minas Gîl (total: 3)\030Collect choice cuts of spider from the Scuttledells (total: 4)\tBingo has tried to translate the locations mentioned in the recipe book where you might find the ingredients for the breakfast: Marshy taters can be found on the edge of foetid pools in the middle of the Drownholt. Sage bushes grow at the Wild Ruin, south of Ost Galadh, in Emyn Lûm. Mirkwood crows can be found around Emyn Lûm, and spiders can be found in the Scuttledells. Sprigs of mint grow around the tower of Minas Gîl, east of Ost Galadh.\n2\tBring the breakfast ingredients to Bingo in the Haunted Inn\tBingo is inside the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood. You have collected the ingredients Bingo will need to prepare the breakfast he wants, and should bring them back to him.\n3\tTalk to Prestadír in the Haunted Inn\tPrestadír is inside the Haunted Inn, located within the Dourstocks of Mirkwood. Bingo has asked you to see if any of the other Rangers know where Aduiallin has gone.\n4\tTalk to Bingo in the Haunted Inn\tBingo is inside the Haunted Inn, within the Dourstocks of Mirkwood. Prestadír claims to have never heard of a Ranger named Aduiallin before.\n5\tTalk to Adolinda in the Haunted Inn\tAdolinda is in a shadowy corner of the Haunted Inn.\n6\tTalk to Bingo in the Haunted Inn\tBingo is in the Haunted Inn, located in the Dourstocks of Mirkwood. You have learned that Adolinda is not a Ranger at all, but is instead a resident of Audaghaim lingering beneath a curse from long ago.\n",
[5340]="70040EE4\n1\tCollect fresh fish from the docks (total: 6)\tToday's catch of fresh fish can be found along the piers where the boats are parked in the wharf of Dol Amroth. You should pick up the fresh fish from the wharf, and bring it to Anírwen.\n2\tBring the fish to Anírwen\tAnírwen is at the market near the docks of Dol Amroth, on the eastern side of the city. You should bring the fresh catch to Anírwen.\n",
[5341]="7005977D\n1\tFish for wild minnows in the Wildwood (total: 6)\tWild minnows can be found in the ponds of the Wildwood. You should fish for wild minnows.\n2\tPlace the wild minnows in a storage crate\tA storage crate can be found in either Trader's Wharf or Trestlebridge. You should place the wild minnows in a storage crate.\n",
[5342]="7000F493\n1\tTalk to Nokki\tNoglond is south of Thorin's Hall, south and east of the Vale of Thrain, along the road to the Low Lands. Refkell has asked that you visit Nokki and tell him of his latest catch.\n",
[5343]="7000EC0F\n1\tOlavi's fish-buckets can be found south-west of his camp along the Ice Bay. Fearing the bears, Olavi has asked you to retrieve his fish-buckets from the fishing-grounds.\t\n2\tBring the fish buckets to Olavi\030Collect buckets of fish (total: 5)\tOlavi is at his fishing camp east of Sûri-kylä along the road in Jä-rannit. You should bring the fish-buckets you recovered to Olavi.\n",
[5344]="7000EC10\n1\tCollect Olavi's fishing pole\tThere are Angmarim along the shore of the Ice Bay, south-west of Olavi's camp along the bay. Olavi has asked you to recover his fishing-pole from the Angmarim.\n2\tTalk to Olavi\030Collect Fishing-rod\tOlavi is at his camp along the road in Jä-rannit. You have recovered Olavi's fishing-pole and should return it to him at once.\n",
})
